16.4M S OF RADIAL F.O.C. OF 60 AVE; 18.2M S OF S F.O.C. OF CRONQUIST DR 0.6M S OF MP</groundspeak:encoded_hints>
      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="683821030">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-02T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP716 - Cronquist Drive - this one took longer to get to than to find, silly alley blocking guy! &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Road trip! Iron Phoenix and I had a fantastic caching and capping from Calgary to Red Deer. Thanks for the work you do maintaining the caps outforthehunt.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683667970">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-02T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP716 - Cronquist Drive&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for another day of capping and caching with OBA, this time in Red Deer!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; After finally getting up the right alley to get next to the cap (and have a place to stop the car!) it wasn't too hard to find.  We missed the first turn in and when we got to the second, someone had the entire alley way blocked with their monstrous gate! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_shock.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Thankfully the next way we tried worked and we pulled right up.  TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683268559">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-02T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="12442378">mikefromcanmore</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP716 Cronquist Drive  Toughest part of this one was finding a place to park.  The back alley is your friend on this one.  Cap was quickly found.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="681996301">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-29T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="553001">Bearberrys Cub</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP716 Cronquist Drive

N 52° 15.580 W 113° 50.256&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I wasn't really sure I was going to go to Red Deer this morning until I got up, checked the weather and the brass cap page. Even though the forecast was for some rain, the temperatures were supposed to hit the double digits so I decided to go.   Since I was not familiar with navigating around Red Deer, I had some back and forth but all in all it wasn’t too bad.  Most were quick finds, although the surface of some of the caps was unreadable. Pictures have been sent to OFTH.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
